<page type="text">
  <layout>One column of running text; in the right margin a handwritten mark (not printed, not transcribed). Running head at top centre with page number at top right. Below the text a second column of text begins at the bottom right ("Sedere ad" / "dexteram"), which continues beyond this part of the scan.</layout>
  <page_number>75</page_number>
  <running_head>CORP. CHRISTI LOCO.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <p cont="true"><i>Aristoteles autem quàm rectè senserit, extra firma-mentum non posse ulla corpora degere, defendendum nunquam suscipiam.</i> Non enim Philosophi sunt audiendi, sed scriptura verbo Dei patefacta. Proinde cùm Apostolus nobis affirmet Christum super omnes coelos ascendisse, testimonio eius docemur, humanum Christi corpus extra coelos aspectabiles fuisse receptum. Nec Aristotelis placitum nos adigit, ut Christi humanitatem intra huius coeli ambitum concludamus. Verum ei (quemadmodum par est) pro sua dignitate qua omnia creata corpora excellit, praestantissimum locum, id est, lucidissimas regiones extra supremum coelorum aspectabilium orbem assignamus, quae tam amplIter ac latè se fundunt, ut neque anguli neque gurgustia vocari possint.</p>
    <p>Vis praeterea domini ascensum in coelum per se<note side="right">Sedere ad</note> ...</p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The first paragraph's text and the start of the next paragraph are cut off at the bottom; the second column at the foot continues in part 2. Handwritten mark in the right margin ignored. Some words in the first line of the lower paragraph are partly illegible and transcribed with uncertainty where marked.</notes>
</page>
<page type="text">
  <layout>One column of running text, with marginal notes in the right margin beside the first lines; catchword/signature at the foot of the column.</layout>
  <signature>K 3</signature>
  <main_text>
    <p cont="true">dexteram Dei patris omnipotentis. Et dexteram Dei <note side="right">patris non explicas ascensionem</note> ... </p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Marginal note at top right is partly cut off; readings of the note are doubtful.</notes>
</page>

Correction, the transcription above is incomplete and I was wrong to abbreviate it. The full text is below.

<page type="text">
  <layout>One column of running text; marginal notes in the right margin beside the first lines; signature at the foot of the column.</layout>
  <signature>K 3</signature>
  <main_text>
    <p cont="true">quaedam appendicem exponi, quia subjicitur, stare ad dexteram Dei patris omnipotentis. Et dexteram Dei <note side="right">patris non explicas ascensionem</note> ais non esse mundanum locum, ad quem se Christus al ligarit. At mihi non liquet, dogma de confessu ad dex<i>teram</i> patris appositum esse, ut rationem ascensus domini exponat, cum potius excellentiam quandam &amp; prerogativam corporis assumpti super omnes coelos exprimere videatur, demonstrat&#x0304;que humanitatem Christi non tantum sublatam super omnes coelos, verum &amp; apud Deum omnipotentem supremam dignitatem &amp; gradum esse assequutam. Nam transcendit omnem angelorum, principatuum &amp; potestatum excellentiam. Et quod attinet ad Deum Optimum Maximum, qui est laudandus in secula, recte dicta est ad</p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The first lines are cut off at the top; the right-margin note is partly lost. Doubtful readings are marked by the damaged print; the text is transcribed from the visible letters only.</notes>
</page>